771 </lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7651534</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Boberetal1994"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bober</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Franz</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Arnold</surname><given-names>H.H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Gruss</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Tremblay</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pax-3 is required for the development of limb musclesa possible role for the migration of dermomyotomal muscle progenitor cells</article-title><source>Development.</source><volume>120</volume><year>1994</year><fpage>603</fpage><lpage>612 </lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8162858</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Caplan1991"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Caplan</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mesenchymal stem cells</article-title><source>J. Orthopaed. Res.</source><volume>169</volume><year>1991</year><fpage>641</fpage><lpage>650 </lpage></citation></ref><ref id="ChristandOrdhal1995"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Christ</surname><given-names>B.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ordhal</surname><given-names>C.P.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Early stages of chick somite development</article-title><source>Anat. Embryol.</source><volume>191</volume><year>1995</year><fpage>381</fpage><lpage>396 </lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7625610</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Cooperetal1999"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cooper</surname><given-names>R.N.</given-names></name><name><surname>Tajbakhsh</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Mouly</surname><given-names>V.</given-names></name><name><surname>Cossu</surname><given-names>G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Buckingham</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Butler-Browne</surname><given-names>G.L.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Two distinct pathways of satellite cell activation in regenerating mouse skeletal muscle</article-title><source>J. Cell Sci.</source><volume>112</volume><year>1999</year><fpage>2895</fpage><lpage>2901 </lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10444384</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CornelisonandWold1997"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cornelison</surname><given-names>D.D.W.</given-names></name><name><surname>Wold</surname><given-names>B.J.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Single-cell analysis of regulatory gene expression in quiescent and activated mouse skeletal muscle satellite cells</article-title><source>Dev. Biol.</source><volume>191</volume><year>1997</year><fpage>270</fpage><lpage>283 </lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9398440</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Cossu1997"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cossu</surname><given-names>G.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Unorthodox myogenesispossible developmental significance and implications for tissue histogenesis and regeneration</article-title><source>Histol. Histopathol.</source><volume>12</volume><year>1997</year><fpage>755</fpage><lpage>760 </lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9225158</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CossuandMolinaro1987"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cossu</surname><given-names>G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Molinaro</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cell heterogeneity in the myogenic lineage</article-title><source>Curr. Topics Dev. Biol.</source><volume>23</volume><year>1987</year><fpage>185</fpage><lpag